To build a website for your chess club, you have a few different paths depending on your technical skill and what features you need. 

Here is a complete guide, including a **ready-to-use code template** you can copy and paste right now.

---

### Option 1: The Quick & Free Way (No Code)
If you don't want to code, use one of these platforms and use the text/ideas from the template below:
1. **Lichess or Chess.com:** Both allow you to create "Clubs" for free, which gives you a built-in forum, tournament manager, and member list.
2. **Google Sites or Carrd.co:** Super simple drag-and-drop website builders where you can put your meeting times and location in 10 minutes.
3. **Discord:** Great for online clubs to chat, share puzzles, and organize matches.

---

### Option 2: Build It Yourself (Free Code Template)
If you want your own professional-looking website, you can use the HTML/CSS code below. 

#### How to use this code:
1. Copy the code block below.
2. Paste it into a text editor (like Notepad on Windows or TextEdit on Mac).
3. Save the file as `index.html`.
4. Double-click the file to open it in your web browser!

```html
